# NOTE ON ORDER: in .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern wins. The general
# default therefore comes first and the byte-exact overrides come last.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.se1   binary
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary

# Keep diffs of the derived corpus readable in review.
*.md diff=markdown

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-exact paths -- DO NOT let Git normalise these. Must stay last.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule cards cite the corpus by character offset (`char_span`) and by SHA-256 of
# the quoted text. Those offsets are counted over the file exactly as stored.
#
# With EOL normalisation on, a CRLF working copy becomes LF in the repository
# and LF again on a Linux or macOS checkout -- which shifts every offset in
# Knowledge/phaladeepika.md by up to 5,969 characters. Verification would fail
# on every card, and the repository would be usable only on Windows.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion, so these files round-trip byte for byte
# on every platform. This is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
Knowledge/**                      -text
Rules/**/*.json                   -text
Pipeline/books/**/ocr/*.json      -text
Pipeline/books/**/verified/*.json -text
